Hi,

On Tue, Oct 21, 2014 at 3:28 PM, Gert Doering <gert@...1296...> wrote:

>
> > The MI-GUI solves that problem right now as opposed to sometime in
> future.
>
> True, this should have been integrated much sooner.  We expected a 2.4
> release early 2014, not "maybe q2 2015" or such, but things did not work
> out the way as planned due to lots of personal reasons.


> As we're currently somewhat short on manpower, we're not going to change
> the building of the 2.3 install bundles to include a different GUI and
> explain the difference to people - but if you already do that, build
> installer bundles, we're happy to provide links to your version.
>

I have a small user-base and use a per user customized installer that
includes a user-specific config file and certificate etc..  Currently I
don't have the
resources to maintain a publicly distributable installer -- keeping in sync
with
upstream changes and bug fixes would be a major commitment.  But I can strip
down site-specific configs and make our bundle available as is..

I do not expect you to repackage 2.3 with a new GUI, but If 2.4 will/can
come out
with a front-end that can  run without admin access that would be great..

Best,

Selva

--001a11c2802884ec880505f472c5
